 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "Your city sits on flat, low land between small rivers, and every typhoon floods it.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you build bigger storm drains.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But the drains empty into those small rivers, and the rivers overflow.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So next to each river, you dig a shaft seventy meters deep.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "When a river rises, it spills over a wall and falls down the shaft.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But a hole only holds so much. It fills, and the river floods anyway.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you connect the shafts with a tunnel ten meters wide, fifty meters down.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Six kilometers long. A river flowing under the city.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But that water has to leave, and the big river is up at the surface.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you build a giant tank with fifty-nine pillars, five hundred tons each.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "It slows the rushing water down, so it doesn't wreck what comes next.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Pumps powered by airplane-style turbines, pushing two hundred tons of water every second into the big river.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Japan really built this, north of Tokyo. People call it the underground temple.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Congratulations! You just built a flood tunnel. What should we build next?",
   "pausa": 0.3
  }
 ],
